==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|mura}}, from {{etyl|la|de}} {{m|la|murus||wall}}. Related to  {{etyl|en|-}} {{m|en|mure}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmaʊ̯ɐ/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Mauer.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|aʊ̯ɐ|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Mauern|Mäuerchen}}

# artificially created [[wall]]
## {{label|de|specifically}} The [[Berlin Wall]].

====Usage notes====
* See {{m|de|Wand}} for notes on the distinction between ''Mauer'' and this widely synonymous word.

